Sure all the dlc's are expensive, but imho only for EUIV you actually get your money's worth of all the >30$ games.
a) You get to right all the historical wrongs you inherited;
b) Distorted guitars and double bass drum excort your armies into havoc of thirty-years war;
c) Who would have guessed that XVI century India is a fun place for an unscrupulous leader.
EUIV is truly "The Wire" of video games.

A proper sequel of Assassin's Creed 1, AC2 shows little changes in its setup.
Pros:
+ nice graphics, even if a bit simple (realism?);
+ very nice idea of having your own personal base - luna park;
+ also, value to arts and history, which is poorly felt nowadays;
+ exciting exploration of (fictional) templar crypts;
+ mind-blowing final plot twist which turns your head upside down and inside-out;
+ fun glyphs minigames, help break the monotony;
+ maybe a bit less simple than AC1 - some missions require planning, which is good.
Cons:
- feather quest in AC2 = templar flag quest in AC1. So much pain in the bass, very poor reward;
- races are sometimes frustrating for their request of absolute perfection;
- same old story, final plot twist aside: I was more excited in the "real world" sketches;
- the PC is a lady killer bachelor and when he is surrounded by ♥♥♥♥♥♥♥♥♥♥s he is embarassed. I would have liked the possibility of hiring them (not necessarily with cut-scenes), to add flavour to the character - no, he is a jesuite in the inside and you have no option of changing it;
Recommended - for those who like this kind of game. Otherwise, try and test it before buying: once you play the first 3 - 5 hours you know how you will play for the rest of the game.

[POSSIBLE SPOILERS for anyone wanting to go in completely blind] Oneshot is amazing. I thought it would be appropriate to start with that. Oneshot will make you laugh, it will make you smile and really enjoy yourself, and then it might take you to the other side of the spectrum. This game is truly a masterpiece of storytelling. It really gets you to like the characters and makes you want them to succeed. It keeps you uneasy about the reason for your quest and the possible outcome. I wholeheartedly recommend this game. The graphics are cute and enjoyable, the full-screen art is fantastic and cute, the characters are deep even if they don't get a lot for their backstories - actually, let's talk about that. Honestly, that's my only gripe with this game. It's way too short. I started this expecting to get 4-6 hours out of it atleast, but my first playthrough took about 2 hours. Because of the short amount of time to present the world and those living in it, some of the characters and areas just seem kind of unpolished and forgettable. This game would be a million times better if it took its time to explore each character and expand on each location more. Now, that's the only problem I had with this game. I REALLY enjoyed the entire 2 (and 1/2 to
) Playthroughs I did. PLEASE buy this game to benefit yourself and the developers, you won't regret it!
After the recent soltice update I wanted to update this review, however I promise I won't spoil anything: The new update and subsequently new ending makes this game a lot more enjoyable. The new ending feels more satisfactory, like you actually accomplished something, and it will definitely leave you in tears. At this point I can't recommend this game enough.
